   "text": "The image shows a rifamycin-type ansa macrolide fused to a phenoxazine, i.e. a benzoxazino-rifamycin, with a 3-(dimethylamino)prop-1-ynyl group on the benzo ring.\n\n**Core**\n- The naphthoquinone-furanone core carries the amide NH, a C=O, a phenolic OH and an aryl methyl.\n- The quinone ring is fused to the phenoxazine: one carbon bears N= and the neighbouring carbon bears the ring O.\n- The alkyne carbon sits meta to the carbon bearing the phenoxazine O.\n\n**Ansa chain**\n- Starting from the amide C=O, the chain runs C(CH3)=CH\u2013CH=CH\u2013CH(CH3)\u2013CH(OH)\u2013CH(CH3)\u2013CH(OH)\u2013CH(CH3)\u2013CH(OAc)\u2013CH(CH3)\u2013CH(OMe)\u2013CH=CH\u2013O.\n- The chain ends at the quaternary carbon of the furanone, which carries a methyl group.\n\n**Stereochemistry**\n- The wedge and hash tags and the E/Z geometry of the chain were not read independently from the drawing. I copied them from the rifampicin-type ansa chain as I remember its SMILES, so they are less certain than the connectivity.\n- Only the quaternary stereocentre was re-derived: its neighbour order differs from the reference, so I recomputed the tag.\n\nThe ring-closure numbers and branch parentheses were checked by hand for validity, not by a parser.\n\nSMILES: C[C@H]1/C=C/C=C(/C(=O)NC2=C3Oc4cc(C#CCN(C)C)ccc4N=C3C4=C5C(=O)[C@@](C)(O/C=C/[C@@H]([C@H]([C@H]([C@@H]([C@@H]([C@@H]([C@H]1O)C)O)C)OC(=O)C)C)OC)OC5=C(C)C(O)=C4C2=O)\\C"
